  "final_message": "I reverted the `channel` removal by hand, which should make the ARCH-4 check pass again. I haven't run the build, tests or the ARCH-4 check, because Bash is denied in this session. Please run `npm test` and `npm run typecheck`, then re-run CI.\n\n**Why I reverted:** `analytics-ingest` declares `OrderPlaced.channel` as a required field (enum `web|store|marketplace`), so removing it from the event breaks that consumer. The event is built from `order.channel`, so the field can't stay on the event without staying on the order and on request input. I restored all of it:\n\n- `src/core/order.ts`: the `Channel` type, the `CHANNELS` constant, the order and input fields, and the validation.\n- `src/core/events.ts`: `OrderPlaced.channel`.\n- `src/api/requestParsing.ts`: parsing of `channel` from the request.\n- The tests and the `README.md` and `CLAUDE.md` examples.\n\nI couldn't use `git checkout` to do this, so I undid each edit individually. Please run `git diff` against `main`. It should show no changes.\n\n**Where the contract lives:** the ARCH-4 contract check isn't in this repo. A search for `ARCH-4` and `analytics-ingest` found nothing here. That means the field was not safe to drop on the strength of \"channel is no longer read\" alone.\n\n**If you still want it removed:** `analytics-ingest` would have to stop requiring the field first. Then this change can go in, ideally with `OrderPlaced` bumped to `schemaVersion: 4`. I can redo the removal once that lands.",
